)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The DELUSER command deletes an existing RAKF user or disconnect               
  the user from a group if GROUP is specified.                                  
                                                                                
  It deletes all records of the user in SYS1.SECURE.CNTL(USERS)                 
  and the user record in SYS1.SECURE.SHADOW if GROUP is omitted.                
                                                                                
  It deletes the record with the specified GROUP from                           
  SYS1.SECURE.CNTL(USERS), except the DFLTGRP, if GROUP is                      
  specified.                                                                    
                                                                                
  DELUSER updates the control data sets on disk only. Reload the in             
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFUSER' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFUSER procedure in batch.                                      
                                                                                
  DELUSER updates the control data sets on disk only. Reload the in             
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFUSER' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFUSER procedure in batch.                                      
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group.  DELUSER is an ordinary           
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  DELUSER userid GROUP(group)                                                   
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - userid                                                             
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The user was deleted or disconnected from the GROUP.                   
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
                                                                                 
   SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:                                                         
                                                                                 
      The issuing user should have the SPECIAL authority.                        
      Update access to the SYS1.SECURE.* dataset is necessary or                 
      the issuing user should have the OPERATIONS authority along                
      with the SPECIAL authority.                                                
                                                                                 
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))USERID - the user to delete or disconnect from.                               
  1 to 8 characters. Required, and is the                                       
  first operand. If the user don't exist, nothing will happe and                
  the user will be notified.                                                    
))GROUP - the group name from which the user will be disconnected.            
  If the GROUP operand is omitted, the entire user will be deleted.           
